  "item:mb-waves-1-04": "",
  "item:mb-waves-1-05": "division-unguarded|question|args[0].args[1]|Division whose divisor (t, 2) has no stated non-vanishing side condition. This is a question, not a defect: the divisor may well be non-zero and simply unstated. ;; division-unguarded|question|args[1].args[0].args[1]|Division whose divisor (m) has no stated non-vanishing side condition. This is a question, not a defect: the divisor may well be non-zero and simply unstated. ;; division-unguarded|question|args[1].args[1].args[1]|Division whose divisor (x, 2) has no stated non-vanishing side condition. This is a question, not a defect: the divisor may well be non-zero and simply unstated.",
  "item:mb-waves-1-06": "division-unguarded|question|args[1].args[1]|Division whose divisor (c) has no stated non-vanishing side condition. This is a question, not a defect: the divisor may well be non-zero and simply unstated. ;; squaring-adds-solutions|question|args[1].args[0].args[0].args[0]|Two terms raised to the same even power (2) are equated. Raising a relation to an even power admits the sign-flipped branch, so a side condition fixing the sign is needed for the step to be reversible.",
